{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.AlgebraMap","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.no_odd_rung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.no_odd_rung","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L92-L97","doc":"Every odd order vanishes, not just the cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.no_cubic_rung","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.no_cubic_rung","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L83-L90","doc":"**No cubic rung (derived).**  The geometric NZ series has no `u³` term:\nparity kills every odd order.  This is the proved invariant behind the\nscope-(b) exclusion of \"S·u³ as a geometric NZ coefficient\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.NeumannZagierEvenPotential.even_potential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.NeumannZagierEvenPotential.even_potential","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L81-L81","doc":"NZ parity: the potential is even as a function of `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.NeumannZagierEvenPotential.potential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.NeumannZagierEvenPotential.potential","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L79-L79","doc":"A finite truncation of the NZ potential series in the deformation\nvariable `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.NeumannZagierEvenPotential.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.NeumannZagierEvenPotential.mk","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.NeumannZagierEvenPotential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.NeumannZagierEvenPotential","kind":"class","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L70-L81","doc":"**Neumann–Zagier even-potential data (§3b-cond hypothesis class).**\n\nThe single field is NZ85's parity result for the chosen truncation: the\npotential is even as a function.  An instance for a specific manifold is\nsupplied by the NZ theorem (v(u) odd); we do not fabricate one here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.two_torsion_free_of_noZeroDivisors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.two_torsion_free_of_noZeroDivisors","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L64-L68","doc":"Two-torsion-freeness from the standard typeclasses: in a ring with no\nzero divisors where `2 ≠ 0`, `2·r = 0` forces `r = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.coeff_odd_eq_zero_of_comp_neg_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.coeff_odd_eq_zero_of_comp_neg_eq","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L54-L62","doc":"An even polynomial (as a function: `p(−X) = p`) has vanishing odd\ncoefficients, provided `R` has no 2-torsion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.coeff_comp_neg_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.NeumannZagierParity.coeff_comp_neg_X","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/NeumannZagierParity.lean#L39-L52","doc":"Coefficient of the reflected polynomial: `(p.comp (−X)).coeff n = (−1)ⁿ · p.coeff n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}